00:00:05.749 --> 00:00:07.110 align:start position:0%
welcome to the hugging face task series  in this video we'll take a look at the  image classification task  image classification is the task of  assigning a class to an image image  classification models take an image as  an input and return a class label  the model assumes that images only  contain one class instance per image  image classification models are  evaluated on the usual classification  metrics in addition to a more obvious  metric like accuracy a common metric  used is the f1 score which is calculated  over the average of two metrics called  precision and recall  the f1 score takes into consideration  class imbalance in your data set so it's  a better indication of how your model is  making predictions across an imbalanced  data set an example data set used for  this task is scifar  here we can see each image is paired  with its associated label  image classification is used for a wide  range of problems from medical imaging  to remote sensing  an example application is determining  whether a ct scan contains cancerous  tissues or not  for more information on the image  classification task check out the task  pages
 

